# Rendered by vm/bootstrap.sh -> /etc/blog/app.env (root:root 0400) and passed
# to the container with EnvironmentFile=.
#
# Intentionally empty. The app image is a static file server (image/app/) whose
# whole configuration -- port, root, cache headers -- is baked into the image
# at build time, and the site has no secrets. The file still has to exist
# because the quadlet names it.
#
# Format if that ever changes: KEY=VALUE, one per line. podman takes values
# literally -- no quotes, no shell expansion. Substituted: ${DOMAIN}
# ${APP_PORT} ${APP_DATA_PATH} ${TRUSTED_PROXIES} and ${SECRET_<NAME>} for each
# id in infra/secret-names.txt.
